From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 21:55:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(auth): stop birthDate dead-end from blocking cardio
 objective creation

Reported bug: creating a cardio "objetivo" would throw "confirme a data de
nascimento no perfil" for accounts with a missing/blank birthDate -- but
ProfileNew.tsx (the actual Profile screen) has no birthDate field at all,
and AuthGuard's "COMPLETE SEU PERFIL" completion screen (the only place
that ever collects birthDate outside registration) only reopened when
termsAccepted was missing, never when birthDate specifically was missing.
Any account with termsAccepted=true but no birthDate (legacy accounts,
partial/social-login onboarding) was permanently stuck with no in-app way
to fix it.

Fix: AuthGuard's completion gate now also reopens when birthDate is
missing, and pre-fills whatever the account already has (cpf, height,
weight, city, state, sex) so a person who's only missing birthDate isn't
forced to retype everything else. The server-side adult-only check in
cardio-objective.ts stays intact as defense in depth (never removed a
minor-safety gate) but its error message no longer points to a
nonexistent profile field.

